6-bit EXL3 decodeGroup + zero-copy y_stride for stitched Flash Next projections

Extends TensorFold's EXL3 projection-group kernel (`tf_exl3_group`) from 4-bit
(`halves == 8`) to 6-bit `mul1` (`halves == 12`, `tf_exl3_group_12_2_{4,8}`),
and adds `y_stride` directly to `LinearArgs` so stitched decode projections
(`in_proj_qkv+z`, `q+k+v`) write straight into `pa` with zero `exl3_tmp` and
zero `copyCols` launches (-108 launches/round). Gated by `TF_EXL3_DECODE_GROUP`
and `TF_EXL3_GROUP_STRIDED` (both default 1).

Verified on GB10 (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 4.05bpw + DFlash2):
- 1-stream decode: +2.3-3.4% from 6-bit grouping + consistent N=1 gain from y_stride
  (code 97.5, prose 53.2, devops 89.0, json 109.7 tok/s)
- Exactness: 4/4 greedy & 4/4 T=0.7 token_sha256 identical, drafts on == drafts off.

